<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Narsinghgarh State</h1><p class="st-meta">1681 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Narsinghgarh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Umat Parmar Rajput state of Malwa, split from Rajgarh in 1681 and ruled from its lake-side capital.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Narsinghgarh was formed in 1681 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paras-ram">Paras Ram</a>, a member of the Umat Parmar ruling house of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rajgarh-state">Rajgarh</a>, separated part of the family lands. The capital, Narsinghgarh, was built beside a lake among the hills.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Rajas ruled a plateau territory of wheat and opium farmers. In the 18th century they paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>, and under British paramountcy after 1818 the state was an eleven-gun salute state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhopal-agency">Bhopal Agency</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Narsinghgarh joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madhya-bharat">Madhya Bharat</a> in 1948 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956. The town lies in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rajgarh-state">Rajgarh</a> district.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/narsinghgarh-state.jpg" alt="Narsinghgarh State" width="320" height="211"><figcaption>Image: QuadrangleDinglePingle · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narsinghgarh_Flag.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1681 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Narsinghgarh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Paras Ram</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malvi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Narsinghgarh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=narsinghgarh-state" aria-label="Narsinghgarh State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6794 1294 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Narsinghgarh State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7114 1550L7364 1601M7114 1550L7364 1602M7114 1550L7064 1471"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7064 1471h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7114 1550h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7114 1550h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=narsinghgarh-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
